  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_009 (pca_n2000 + resnet50, concat, singleprofile) is the best so far at 0.527 acc, clearly outperforming both the RNA-only baseline (config_007, 0.485) and the scgpt variant (config_004, 0.427). This establishes pca_n2000 + resnet50 + concat as a strong backbone. Uncertainty: All three completed experiments use singleprofile; we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile + aggregation adds value. Question: config_010 extends the best-known configuration by moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation, while keeping the proven RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion (concat) fixed. This isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation as the primary new variable. Why best: It is the most natural exploitation of our strongest evidence while exploring the single largest untested design dimension (profile setting). Testing multiprofile now, before investing in further fusion or image-encoder variants, tells us whether the added complexity of multi-profile aggregation is worthwhile, which will shape all subsequent experiments."
}

